# This file is load-bearing, not hygiene. It changes what the build PRODUCES.
#
# The Dockerfile does `COPY package.json package-lock.json ./` -> `npm ci` ->
# `COPY . .`. Without `node_modules/` excluded, that second copy drops the
# HOST's node_modules straight on top of the tree `npm ci` just built from the
# lockfile - silently replacing a reproducible install with whatever is on the
# developer's disk, possibly built for a different architecture, and busting
# the layer cache on every build.
#
# `dist/` matters for the same reason: a stale host build would be copied in
# and then overwritten by `npm run build`, which is merely wasteful - but if
# the build ever failed, the stale bundle is what would ship.

node_modules/
dist/
build/
.vite/

.git/
.gitignore
.dockerignore
Dockerfile
README.md

coverage/
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# Never let local environment files into an image. The bundle needs none of
# them - there are no VITE_* variables in this app by design - so anything
# matching here would be a mistake travelling to a registry.
.env
.env.*
